          ],
          "content": "Also, it is given that"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.353,
            0.173,
            0.897,
            0.192
          ],
          "content": "\\angle \\mathrm{PST} = \\angle \\mathrm{PRQ}\\tag{2}",
          "image_source": "images/page_11_equation_3.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.199,
            0.135,
            0.217
          ],
          "content": "So,"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.347,
            0.198,
            0.717,
            0.218
          ],
          "content": "$\\angle \\mathrm{PRQ} = \\angle \\mathrm{PQR}$ [From (1) and (2)]"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.224,
            0.205,
            0.243
          ],
          "content": "Therefore,"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.385,
            0.223,
            0.851,
            0.244
          ],
          "content": "PQ = PR (Sides opposite the equal angles)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.249,
            0.437,
            0.268
          ],
          "content": "i.e., PQR is an isosceles triangle."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.412,
            0.294,
            0.587,
            0.313
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "EXERCISE 6.2"
        },
        {
